This client talks to a MeshCentral server using the same control-channel messages as the
MeshCentral web interface. The following parts follow MeshCentral's source code:

  * mcdesktop/rights.py: the account and device permission rules are a port of the web
    interface functions GetMeshRights, GetNodeRights and removeUserRights
    (views/default.handlebars) and of the matching checks in meshuser.js.
  * mcdesktop/info_panel.py: the agent type names (agentsStr in the web interface).
  * mcdesktop/user_panel.py, group_panel.py, admin_panel.py: the wording and bit values of the
    permission, feature and consent options, and the user list export columns, match the web
    interface so that both clients show the same information.

The remote desktop view embeds the MeshCentral web viewer that is served by the user's own
MeshCentral server at run time. That viewer is not copied into or distributed with this project.
